\",\n+    \"remote_branch_search\": \"no match before checkpoint\",\n+    \"pinned_statement_duplicates\": \"only this ID matched the periodic-points nonempty-interior statement\",\n+    \"separate_prior_report\": \"no matching research-results entry\"\n+  },\n+  \"sources\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"owr2020-12.pdf\",\n+      \"url\": \"https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46848\",\n+      \"scope\": \"Original contribution pp.668\\u2013669; Questions 1\\u20132; workshop 1\\u20137 March 2020\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"aa7e1c6da8d3f04fcb48c8e4ca16ef93e718e88fb690e47855a4f481871774ec\",\n+      \"bytes\": 672109\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"kozhasov-kummer-v1.pdf\",\n+      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2004.10003v1\",\n+      \"scope\": \"21 April 2020; Theorem 2 p.2, proof Section 2.2 p.6; full-interior assertion also in abstract/introduction\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"ace89da93222d9e9c26d937e22e7176291e866f08c79d9b5cd0fff501db2132c\",\n+      \"bytes\": 718174\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"kozhasov-kummer.pdf\",\n+      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2004.10003v2\",\n+      \"scope\": \"27 October 2020; Example 1 p.3, Theorem 2, Lemma 9, proof of Theorem 3 p.6\",\n+      \"sha256\": \"e19b6fa372eee88705efb610b4892bd325ae609e62fc680cef392edf4220defb\",\n+      \"bytes\": 164773\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"journal_publication\": \"not verified; source described as preprint\",\n+  \"known_solution_credit\": [\n+    \"Khazhgali Kozhasov\",\n+    \"Mario Kummer\"\n+  ],\n+  \"recommended_status\": \"already_solved\",\n+  \"novelty_claim\": false,\n+  \"artifact_sha256\": \"a0d374da6984537cd9902e2e790177791739bdc32ea820b74830a6b50241ea6c\",\n+  \"verification_assertions_passed\": 51,\n+  \"independent_review\": {\n+    \"verdict\": \"PASS_KNOWN_RESULT_EXACT_SCOPE\",\n+    \"report\": \"independent_review/REVIEW.md\",\n+    \"reviewed_artifact_sha256\": \"a0d374da6984537cd9902e2e790177791739bdc32ea820b74830a6b50241ea6c\",\n+    \"review_sha256\": \"5b7967fb26a229d1d86252114063e6097ab6c072acaeed2e7f14baf2e6c528b6\",\n+    \"independent_checks_passed\": 848,\n+    \"mandatory_corrections\": []\n+  },\n+  \"source_audit_completion_estimate_percent\": 100\n+}"},{"sha":"587cbe7d99861345e8e8e7b8ddaadf9cbdb7f95c","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004438/source_record.json","status":"added","additions":68,"deletions":0,"changes":68,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fsource_record.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fsource_record.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fsource_record.json?ref=a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@\n+{\n+  \"id\": 30004438,\n+  \"problem_number\": \"OWR-17475-003\",\n+  \"title\": \"Real Rational Maps with Exclusively Real Periodic Points\",\n+  \"statement\": \"For $d\\\\geq2$, let $\\\\mathcal R_d$ be the set of real morphisms $\\\\phi:\\\\mathbb P^1\\\\to\\\\mathbb P^1$ of degree $d$ whose periodic points are all real. The existence question has an affirmative answer via Chebyshev maps; does $\\\\mathcal R_d$ have full dimension, equivalently nonempty interior, in the space of real degree-$d$ morphisms?\",\n+  \"background\": \"Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\\n\\n**Source report:** [Real Algebraic Geometry with a View Toward Hyperbolic Programming and Free Probability (2021), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2020/12, pp. 639--712](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/12)\\n\\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-22)\\n\\n**Status:** partially solved\\n\\n**Assessment.** The existence part is solved affirmatively by the Chebyshev morphism, which has only real periodic points. The question whether the corresponding locus has nonempty interior or full dimension remains open; only lower-dimensional families are known.\\n\\n**Sources checked.**\\n\\n- [Kozhasov--Kummer (2020)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.10003)\\n- [Oberwolfach Report 12/2020](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/12)\\n\\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.\",\n+  \"difficulty_level_id\": 3,\n+  \"status\": \"partially_solved\",\n+  \"proposed_by\": null,\n+  \"proposed_year\": 2020,\n+  \"category_id\": 11,\n+  \"set_id\": 15,\n+  \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/12\",\n+  \"source_citation\": \"Real Algebraic Geometry with a View Toward Hyperbolic Programming and Free Probability (2021), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2020/12, pp. 639--712\",\n+  \"literature_assessment\": \"The existence part is solved affirmatively by the Chebyshev morphism, which has only real periodic points. The question whether the corresponding locus has nonempty interior or full dimension remains open; only lower-dimensional families are known.\",\n+  \"literature_sources\": [\n+    {\n+      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.10003\",\n+      \"label\": \"Kozhasov--Kummer (2020)\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/12\",\n+      \"label\": \"Oberwolfach Report 12/2020\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"literature_checked_at\": \"2026-08-22\",\n+  \"tags\": [\n+    \"owr\",\n+    \"oberwolfach-reports\",\n+    \"OWR-17475-003\",\n+    \"literature-status:partially-solved\",\n+    \"owr-year:2020\"\n+  ],\n+  \"view_count\": 0,\n+  \"favorite_count\": 0,\n+  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-25T00:00:00Z\",\n+  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-16T12:06:53Z\",\n+  \"published\": true,\n+  \"category\": {\n+    \"id\": 11,\n+    \"name\": \"dynamical_systems\",\n+    \"display_name\": \"Dynamical Systems\",\n+    \"description\": \"Problems about long-term behavior of deterministic systems, Hamiltonian dynamics, and periodic orbits.\",\n+    \"slug\": \"dynamical-systems\",\n+    \"order_index\": 11,\n+    \"created_at\": \"2026-07-31T15:26:25.671Z\"\n+  },\n+  \"difficulty\": {\n+    \"id\": 3,\n+    \"level\": 3,\n+    \"name\": \"L3: Advanced\",\n+    \"description\": \"Difficult problems requiring specialized knowledge and sophisticated techniques.\",\n+    \"color_class\": \"text-yellow-600 bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-200\"\n+  },\n+  \"set\": {\n+    \"id\": 15,\n+    \"name\": \"oberwolfach_reports_open_problems\",\n+    \"display_name\": \"Oberwolfach Reports Open Problems\",\n+    \"description\": \"Open and partially solved problems extracted from Oberwolfach Reports workshop discussions, with report provenance and dated literature assessments.\",\n+    \"slug\": \"oberwolfach-reports-open-problems\",\n+    \"order_index\": 15,\n+    \"created_at\": \"2026-08-25T00:00:00Z\"\n+  },\n+  \"original_statement\": \"For d\\\\ge2, does there exist a real morphism \\\\phi:\\\\mathbb{P}^1\\\\to\\\\mathbb{P}^1 of degree d with only real periodic points, and does the set of such real morphisms have full dimension, equivalently nonempty interior, in the space of all real degree-d morphisms?\",\n+  \"clean_statement\": \"For $d\\\\geq2$, let $\\\\mathcal R_d$ be the set of real morphisms $\\\\phi:\\\\mathbb P^1\\\\to\\\\mathbb P^1$ of degree $d$ whose periodic points are all real. The existence question has an affirmative answer via Chebyshev maps; does $\\\\mathcal R_d$ have full dimension, equivalently nonempty interior, in the space of real degree-$d$ morphisms?\",\n+  \"statement_status\": \"corrected_verified\",\n+  \"statement_verification\": \"The official report was checked. The solved existence clause is distinguished from the remaining full-dimension question.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"ffe28a008ea859bcd797b4d68ee34675f049163c","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004438/turns.json","status":"added","additions":14,"deletions":0,"changes":14,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fturns.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fturns.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fturns.json?ref=a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@\n+{\n+  \"problem_id\": 30004438,\n+  \"problem_number\": \"OWR-17475-003\",\n+  \"turn_limit\": 5,\n+  \"substantive_turns_used\": 0,\n+  \"source_verification_responses\": 1,\n+  \"outcome\": \"known_result_source_correction\",\n+  \"recommended_status\": \"already_solved\",\n+  \"model\": \"gpt-6-astra\",\n+  \"reasoning_effort\": \"xhigh\",\n+  \"explanation\": \"The exact existing theorem was located before pursuing a new proof. The saved exposition and exact checks verify its known construction and ambient/all-period scope. No novelty is claimed.\",\n+  \"independent_review\": \"PASS_KNOWN_RESULT_EXACT_SCOPE\",\n+  \"queue_update_owner\": \"coordinating agent\"\n+}"},{"sha":"49eb67c42bfd19837922f3131d9ef8388d0c0f2c","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004438/verification.json","status":"added","additions":59,"deletions":0,"changes":59,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fverification.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fverification.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fverification.json?ref=a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@\n+{\n+  \"passed\": 51,\n+  \"failed\": 0,\n+  \"sympy_version\": \"1.14.0\",\n+  \"checks\": {\n+    \"d2_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_positive_coefficients\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_negative_residues\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_partial_fractions\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_all_fixed_points_real\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_iterate2_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_iterate2_positive\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_iterate2_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_iterate2_real_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d2_iterate2_real_fixed_points\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_positive_coefficients\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_negative_residues\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_partial_fractions\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_all_fixed_points_real\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_iterate2_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_iterate2_positive\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_iterate2_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_iterate2_real_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d3_iterate2_real_fixed_points\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_positive_coefficients\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_negative_residues\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_partial_fractions\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_all_fixed_points_real\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_iterate2_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_iterate2_positive\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_iterate2_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_iterate2_real_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d4_iterate2_real_fixed_points\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d5_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d5_positive_coefficients\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d5_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d5_negative_residues\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d5_partial_fractions\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d5_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d5_all_fixed_points_real\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d6_degrees\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d6_positive_coefficients\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d6_coprime\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d6_negative_residues\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d6_partial_fractions\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d6_simple_poles\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"d6_all_fixed_points_real\": \"PASS\",\n+    \"single_residue_imaginary_identity\": \"PASS\"\n+  },\n+  \"scope\": \"Finite exact controls of an existing all-degree, all-period proof; not a novelty claim or exhaustive periodic-point test.\"\n+}"},{"sha":"789b9cf69bdfd413c3465c3483ea24fbfc1b85f6","filename":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004438/verify.py","status":"added","additions":35,"deletions":0,"changes":35,"blob_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fverify.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/raw/a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fverify.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/contents/unsolved_math_prioritization%2Fattempts%2F30004438%2Fverify.py?ref=a39d178b10f75fb127058b08e0d0002b3ae97f8a","patch":"@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@\n+#!/usr/bin/env python3\n+\"\"\"Exact checks of a known Kozhasov-Kummer open-family construction.\"\"\"\n+from pathlib import Path\n+import json\n+import sympy as s\n+z=s.symbols('z'); checks={}\n+def ck(name,value):\n+ assert bool(value),name\n+ checks[name]='PASS'\n+def homogeneous_at(poly,p,q,d):\n+ return s.Poly(sum(poly.nth(j)*p.as_expr()**j*q.as_expr()**(d-j) for j in range(d+1)),z)\n+for d in range(2,7):\n+ p=s.Poly(s.prod(z+2*j-1 for j in range(1,d+1)),z)\n+ q=s.Poly(s.prod(z+2*j for j in range(1,d+1)),z)\n+ ck(f'd{d}_degrees',p.degree()==q.degree()==d)\n+ ck(f'd{d}_positive_coefficients',all(a>0 for a in p.all_coeffs()+q.all_coeffs()))\n+ ck(f'd{d}_coprime',s.gcd(p,q).degree()==0)\n+ res=[s.cancel(p.eval(-2*j)/q.diff().eval(-2*j)) for j in range(1,d+1)]\n+ ck(f'd{d}_negative_residues',all(a<0 for a in res))\n+ ck(f'd{d}_partial_fractions',s.cancel(p.as_expr()/q.as_expr()-1-sum(res[j-1]/(z+2*j) for j in range(1,d+1)))==0)\n+ ck(f'd{d}_simple_poles',s.gcd(q,q.diff()).degree()==0)\n+ F=p-s.Poly(z,z)*q\n+ ck(f'd{d}_all_fixed_points_real',F.count_roots(-s.oo,s.oo)==F.degree())\n+ if d<=4:\n+  pp=homogeneous_at(p,p,q,d);qq=homogeneous_at(q,p,q,d);e=d*d\n+  ck(f'd{d}_iterate2_degrees',pp.degree()==qq.degree()==e)\n+  ck(f'd{d}_iterate2_positive',all(a>0 for a in pp.all_coeffs()+qq.all_coeffs()))\n+  ck(f'd{d}_iterate2_coprime',s.gcd(pp,qq).degree()==0)\n+  ck(f'd{d}_iterate2_real_simple_poles',qq.count_roots(-s.oo,s.oo)==e and s.gcd(qq,qq.diff()).degree()==0)\n+  FF=pp-s.Poly(z,z)*qq\n+  ck(f'd{d}_iterate2_real_fixed_points',FF.count_roots(-s.oo,s.oo)==FF.degree())\n+x,y,b,A=s.symbols('x y b A',real=True)\n+ck('single_residue_imaginary_identity',s.simplify(s.im(A/(x+s.I*y-b))+A*y/((x-b)**2+y*y))==0)\n+r={'passed':len(checks),'failed':0,'sympy_version':s.__version__,'checks':checks,'scope':'Finite exact controls of an existing all-degree, all-period proof; not a novelty claim or exhaustive periodic-point test.'}\n+Path(__file__).with_name('verification.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2)+'\\n');print(json.dumps(r,indent=2))"}]]